In order to find the plane, we need to find the two vectors which are perpendicular to the plane and one third of the third. From the last two points, we get $\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\ 4 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ -1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -4 \\ 5 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix}.$  From the third point, we get $\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 5 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ -1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 6 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}.$  Thus we get a normal vector to the plane in the form $\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\ 5 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix} \times \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 6 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -18 \\ -4 \\ 20 \end{pmatrix}$ so we have
\begin{align*}
-18x - 4y + 20z &= D,\\
5x + 6y + 2z &= E,
\end{align*}
where we find $D = -18(0) - 4(-1) + 20(-1) = -18$ and $E = 5(0) + 6(-1) + 2(4) = 2.$  So our equation is $18x + 4y - 20z - 18 = 0.$  The greatest common divisor of the coefficients is 2 and the resulting equation in the form $9x + 2y - 10z - 9 = 0$ is thus our desired answer.

